  "applies_to": "Mitsubishi Electric 9900A series UPS on Modbus TCP, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Mitsubishi 9900A UPS over Modbus TCP: 55 objects (43 AI, 12 BI), all polled. It reads bypass, battery, input and output voltages, currents, frequencies and power, battery capacity and discharge count, module data, the breaker and contactor states, inverter and rectifier operation, battery discharging, UPS fault and ten alarm registers.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Mitsubishi_MUCM_9900_Modbus_TCP_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the Mitsubishi 9900A Modbus TCP register list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Mitsubishi9900A.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "All 55 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Mitsubishi_MUCM_9900_Modbus_TCP",
